# LLM judge configuration (scripts/judge_languages.py / langtrend/llm_client.py).
# Copy to .env and fill in the API key. The uncommented block below is just a
# suggested starting point, not a claim about what's actually deployed — this
# repo's live CI config lives in GitHub Actions Variables/Secrets (Settings >
# Secrets and variables > Actions), which may point at a different provider
# entirely. Check there (or `gh variable list`) for the actual current setup
# rather than assuming from this file.

# OpenRouter free tier (open-weight gpt-oss-20b) via its OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint. Get a key at https://openrouter.ai. Check
# `curl https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models` for the current free-model
# catalog before relying on a specific ID — free-tier listings rotate.
LLM_JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b:free
LLM_JUDGE_API_KEY=
LLM_JUDGE_RPM=20
LLM_JUDGE_RPH=1000

# Cerebras free tier (open-weight gpt-oss-120b) via its OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint. Get a key at https://cloud.cerebras.ai
#LLM_JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.cerebras.ai/v1
#LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-oss-120b
#LLM_JUDGE_API_KEY=
# LLM_JUDGE_RPM=4
# LLM_JUDGE_RPH=150

# Groq free tier now also hosts openai/gpt-oss-120b (same model as above, so
# swapping is behavior-neutral — no need to re-validate prompt output). Get a
# key at https://console.groq.com. Published free-tier limits for this model
# (2026-07): 30 RPM / 1K RPD / 8K TPM / 200K TPD — TPD is the binding one; a
# typical week's judging run is ~0.5-1.2M tokens, so plan on ~3-6 calendar
# days per week via the daily judge-catchup sweep (see langtrend.yml), not a
# single pass. LLM_JUDGE_RPM=4 already keeps requests under the 8K TPM cap.
#LLM_JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
#LLM_JUDGE_API_KEY=
# LLM_JUDGE_RPM=4
# LLM_JUDGE_RPH=150

# Optional fallback chain, tried in order after LLM_JUDGE_MODEL — same
# base_url/key throughout, works with any provider (each attempt is an
# ordinary single-"model" request, not OpenRouter-specific). Each model
# gets its own 3 retries with backoff before chat() moves on to the next
# one in the list; see llm_client.py's chat() docstring. Useful even on a
# single provider, e.g. hopping to a second Groq model if the first's
# per-model TPD quota is spent for the day.
# google/gemma-4-31b-it:free was confirmed present via the live
# `/api/v1/models` check above as of 2026-07-22 — re-verify before use,
# since OpenRouter's free-model catalog rotates.
#LLM_JUDGE_FALLBACK_MODELS=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free

# Local Ollama override for quota-free testing:
#LLM_JUDGE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=qwen3:8b
#LLM_JUDGE_API_KEY=ollama

# Gemini free tier is also OpenAI-compatible, but its free tier explicitly
# trains on submitted content outside the EU/UK/EEA — avoid for paper text:
#LLM_JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Tuning
LLM_JUDGE_TIMEOUT=180
LLM_JUDGE_TEMPERATURE=0
LLM_JUDGE_MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS=12000
LLM_JUDGE_WORKERS=4

# Notification configuration (scripts/notify.sh)
NOTIFY_METHOD=webhook
NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=<your webhook url>
